    "## 17. XGBoost with Class Imbalance Handling\n",
    "\n",
    "XGBoost provides the `scale_pos_weight` parameter for imbalanced binary classification.\n",
    "\n",
    "The weight is calculated from the training data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 37,
   "id": "af88ad84",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Negative samples: 5524\n",
      "Positive samples: 1605\n",
      "Scale positive weight: 3.4417445482866045\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "negative_count = (y_train == 0).sum()\n",
    "positive_count = (y_train == 1).sum()\n",
    "\n",
    "scale_pos_weight = negative_count / positive_count\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Negative samples:\", negative_count)\n",
    "print(\"Positive samples:\", positive_count)\n",
    "print(\"Scale positive weight:\", scale_pos_weight)"
